<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Tobacco up on retail buying.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Tobacco up on retail buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ceylon Tobacco Co Ltd rose 1.8 percent or 50 cents to 28 rupees on retail buying, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share offers good value at current prices which even retailers can afford,&quot; said a local retail broker.</p>
<p>CTC rose to over double its current price when the market rallied in early 1994, he said.</p>
<p>The company has a monopoly on cigarette manufacturing in Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
